  "bios": [
    "Cooking mostly for one, badly, happily.",
    "Weeknight food. Nothing that takes longer than the rice.",
    "Writing down what my parents never measured.",
    "Baker by weekend, spreadsheet by weekday.",
    "I chase texture more than flavour.",
    "Trying to cook through one cookbook a year.",
    "Fermenting things my flatmates have opinions about.",
    "Here to read, not to post.",
    "Feeding four people who agree on nothing.",
    "Ex-restaurant. Recovering.",
    "Everything in one pan or it does not happen.",
    "Learning to cook at 41. It is going fine.",
    "{cuisine} food, mostly, and whatever the market had.",
    "Archiving my grandmother's {cuisine} recipes before they are lost.",
    "Homesick, so I cook {cuisine} on Sundays.",
    "I measure nothing and regret it constantly.",
    "Two knives, one pan, no patience.",
    "Reverse-engineering the {cuisine} dishes I grew up eating.",
    "Saving recipes I will absolutely never cook.",
    "Cooking is the only part of the day nobody emails me about.",
    "Lunchboxes, five days a week, for the last nine years.",
    "A student budget and too many opinions about salt.",
    "Half of these are my mother's. She has approved none of them.",
    "Slow food, fast schedule. It mostly works.",
    "{cuisine} classics, adjusted for a very small kitchen.",
    "I keep the failures in here too."
